summary:
  A rebuild's answer is recognised by its enable alone again, so a hung
  rebuild that answers late is taken for the one sent after it.

history:
  The lock on the loopback rebuild is cleared after thirty seconds without
  an answer, and a rebuild that was waiting goes out. The hung shell is
  still alive and still answers, under the same enable number as its
  successor. Driven with stand-in commands on 2026-11-11: answering last,
  its modules were adopted beside the newer pair, 201,202,301,302 for two
  speakers with a map that knew only 301 and 302. Answering first, it
  released the lock the newer rebuild was still holding.

target:
  package/contents/ui/ReloopLogic.js

find:
      return m !== null && m[1] === String(gen) && m[2] === String(job);

replace:
      return m !== null && m[1] === String(gen);

expect:
  Killed by tst_syncengine::test_a_hung_rebuild_answering_last_is_not_adopted_next_to_its_successor.
  Line-neutral.
